{"title": "Zoom", "description": "Schedule and manage Zoom meetings and participant links.", "examples": ["set up a video call", "share a Zoom meeting link"], "events": [], "tools": ["zoom_create_meeting", "zoom_delete_meeting", "zoom_list_meetings", "zoom_read_meeting", "zoom_reconcile_meeting", "zoom_update_meeting"]}

Create or edit managed Zoom meetings natively. Reuse stable creation keys; reconcile uncertain requests instead of creating duplicates. Create Zoom first, then pass its local managed ID as zoom_meeting_id to calendar_create_event with matching start and duration. The calendar tool automatically appends 'Zoom: <participant join URL>' to your description, adds zoom_meeting_id to metadata, and records the link between the event and meeting; do not also insert the URL into the creation description. Description updates replace the text without reinserting the link, so preserve it when editing. Never disclose host start URLs.
